{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492887,"name":"","username":"LiuChunYin","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/77aa72/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T13:45:15.764Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustom remote MCP OAuth fails before sign-in with: redirect_uri is not allowed by the account configuration. Existing connector Owner Google Tasks MCP remains needsAuth / authentication_required, tools=0. Endpoint: \u003ca href=\"https://tasks-mcp.cecinyin.com/mcp\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eSign in ・ Cloudflare Access\u003c/a\u003e . The server uses Streamable HTTP protected by Cloudflare Access Managed OAuth. Bot diagnostics do not expose the DCR redirect_uris array.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd the remote MCP through Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRequest OAuth authorization on that existing connector.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRegistration fails with the redirect_uri error before the sign-in card opens.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllowlisting the exact /agents/ and then /bot/ callbacks in Cloudflare did not resolve it. No duplicate connector was added; retries have stopped.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOAuth should open the owner sign-in flow, then load MCP tools. Please inspect the failing DCR request and provide the exact redirect_uris array, or correct unintended callback entries. Please confirm the supported callback list for current Grok Bot remote MCP.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot version: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: macOS (darwin)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloudflare allows the following exact HTTPS callback paths on the www subdomain of Cursor:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/agents/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e/bot/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe existing Grok web callback is also allowed. Localhost and 127.0.0.1 callback options are enabled. Both added Cursor callbacks saved successfully. No wildcard or custom scheme was added.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official MCP SDK completed token exchange, tools listing, read-only Google calls, refresh and reconnect. Grok web also completed OAuth and actual read-only tool calls. This does not prove Bot compatibility: Bot has not invoked connection_status or list_tasklists because tools never load.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePossibly related: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/aws-mcp-callback-url-issue/170390\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eAWS MCP callback URL issue\u003c/a\u003e . We have not established that our request has the same root cause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo credentials, authorization codes, full authorization URLs, private task contents or raw logs are included.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492887-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492887-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:20:05.254Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":12,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":60.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/aws-mcp-callback-url-issue/170390","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"AWS MCP callback URL issue","clicks":0},{"url":"https://tasks-mcp.cecinyin.com/mcp","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Sign in ・ Cloudflare Access","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138161,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":492957,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T14:19:42.186Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and for checking the server ahead of time with the official MCP SDK and Grok web. That really narrows things down.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s the full \u003ccode\u003eredirect_uris\u003c/code\u003e array that gets sent during Dynamic Client Registration (it’s the same for desktop and Cloud Agents):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecursor://anysphere.cursor-mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://www.cursor.com/agents/mcp/oauth/callback\u003c/code\u003e (Cloud Agents / web)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttp://localhost:8787/callback\u003c/code\u003e (desktop loopback)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop authorizes via entry 3 (localhost loopback), so your Cloudflare settings for entries 2 and 3 are already correct. The \u003ccode\u003e/bot/\u003c/code\u003e callback you added isn’t related to desktop registrations. It’s harmless, but not needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue is entry 1. Cloudflare Managed OAuth only allows https in “Allowed redirect URIs”, so you can’t allowlist \u003ccode\u003ecursor://\u003c/code\u003e there at all, and Cloudflare rejects the entire registration with \u003ccode\u003eredirect_uri is not allowed by the account configuration\u003c/code\u003e. This isn’t caused by your setup. Your server and config aren’t the problem here. This is an issue on our side that we’re tracking. The goal is for registration to only send https and localhost callbacks. Once that ships, your current Cloudflare configuration should work without any changes. I’ll post an update here when we have one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkaround for now: since it’s your server, you can bypass OAuth using a Cloudflare Access service token. In Zero Trust, create a service token, add a Service Auth policy to the app, and connect MCP using the \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Id\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Secret\u003c/code\u003e headers instead of OAuth (the server needs to accept identity from the Access JWT via the service token). If you try it, let me know whether the tools load.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:19:42.186Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":5.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed/171877/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":492999,"name":"","username":"LiuChunYin","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/77aa72/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T14:49:57.228Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for suggesting Cloudflare Service Tokens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot confirms that \u003ccode\u003eAddMcpServer.headers\u003c/code\u003e supports custom HTTP headers. However, we cannot find a secure way for the owner to enter \u003ccode\u003eCF-Access-Client-Secret\u003c/code\u003e: the connector UI only offers OAuth authentication and account renaming, and the tool schema exposes no secret/vault reference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow can I securely configure this header without putting the secret into chat or model-visible tool arguments?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs there an owner-only settings page, secure credential form, or supported secret reference? Please provide the exact steps for \u003cstrong\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/strong\u003e, rather than Cursor editor’s \u003ccode\u003emcp.json\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is not supported, is there an update on removing the legacy \u003ccode\u003ecursor://\u003c/code\u003e callback from the Bot’s OAuth registration?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T14:49:57.228Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171877,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-custom-mcp-oauth-fails-before-sign-in-redirect-uri-not-allowed","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":fal